# ThinkTogether Frontend - Cursor Rules

## Configuration & Constants

- NEVER use magic strings. Always import from `@/config/constants`
- Use `env.ts` for environment variables: `import { env } from '@/config/env'`
- Use `routes.ts` for navigation: `import { ROUTES } from '@/config/routes'`

## Error Handling

- Always use `handleError()` from `@/lib/errors/error-handler`
- Use custom error classes: `ValidationError`, `AuthenticationError`, etc.
- All error messages in Vietnamese

## API Layer

- Use API services from `@/lib/api/services/`
- Never use raw fetch or axios directly
- All API types in `@/lib/api/types.ts`

## State Management

- Use Zustand stores from `@/stores/` for global state only
- Use React Query for server state
- Use React Hook Form for form state
- Use useState for component-local state
- Always use selectors: `const data = useStore(selectData)`
- Separate actions from state: `actions: { ... }`
- Use devtools and persist middleware

## TypeScript

- Strict types, no `any`
- Use `type` imports: `import type { User } from '@/types'`
- Define interfaces for all props and data structures

## Components

- Use `'use client'` for client components
- Import UI components from `@/shared/ui/`
- One component per file
- Props interface above component

## Validation

- Use Zod schemas for validation
- Use zodResolver with React Hook Form
- All validation messages in Vietnamese

## Localization

- ALL user-facing text in Vietnamese
- Buttons, labels, messages, errors, toasts
- Code comments can be in English

## Code Style

- No XML comments (`/** */`)
- Comment WHY, not WHAT
- Use constants, not magic strings
- Prefer named exports over default exports

## File Organization

```
src/
├── config/         # Constants, env, routes
├── lib/            # API, errors, utils
├── features/       # Feature modules
├── shared/         # Reusable components & hooks
├── stores/         # Zustand stores
└── types/          # Global types
```

## Performance

- Use selectors for Zustand stores
- Lazy load heavy components with `dynamic()`
- Use `useMemo` and `useCallback` when needed

## Testing

- Test utilities and hooks
- Test business logic
- Use descriptive test names

## Before Committing

- [ ] No magic strings
- [ ] Proper error handling
- [ ] TypeScript types defined
- [ ] Vietnamese for user text
- [ ] Use API services
- [ ] Use constants
- [ ] No `any` types



